{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Antiviral", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "A two-chain bacteriocin which requires chain B for optimal activity. The sequence of chain B is SVPTSVYTLGIKILWSAYKHRKTIEKSFNKGFYH. Activity: It inhibits Gram+ bacteria. It also inhibits the flaviviruses Langat and Kunjin, coronavirus SARS-CoV-2, influenza A virus (IAV), and human immunodeficiency virus-1 (HIV-1) (< href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36449554/\">Omer et al., 2022. In addition, downstream of Pln NC8, it is likely there is another two chain bacteriocin named plantaricin J51. Whether it is a true bacteriocin remains to be established ( Diep DB et al, 2009). Updated Jan2023.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Appl Environ Microbiol. 2003 Jan;69(1):383-9", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP01167", "source_id": "AP01167", "source_numeric_id": "01167", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP01167", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Purification and genetic characterization of plantaricin NC8, a novel coculture-inducible two-peptide bacteriocin from Lactobacillus plantarum NC8.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
